Directly reused/adapted upstream material:
- modules/iris/field/IrisField.qml and IrisField.frag -> Widgets/Iris/IrisField.qml
  and Shaders/frag/iris_field.frag. Host imports, explicit frame inputs, shared
  provider ownership and paths adapted. Independent frame insets accommodate
  Hydra's asymmetric bar; an unpainted reference body preserves bar joins with
  separate opacity without painting that bar twice. The fixed light-paper ramp
  follows the lighting slider (100% is upstream-equivalent, zero disables it).
  The frame's metallic lip is bounded by the actual free gutter of Hydra's bar;
  adjoining limits blend at frame corners, without changing the body bevel.
  Inherited Qt opacity is applied once to the completed material, rather than
  separately inside source-over layers; original opaque lighting/shadow solves remain.
  Original SDF, joins, normals, grade, signal and silhouette-shadow equations remain.
- modules/iris/field/IrisGlassBackdrops.qml -> same-named Widgets/Iris singleton,
  adapted with stable owner leases and Qt-guarded references for host teardown.
- modules/iris/field/IrisGlassSource.qml -> Widgets/Iris/IrisGlassSource.qml.
  Hydra wallpaper/cache mapping is supplied by IrisWallpaperView; original
  half-resolution grade-before-blur pipeline retained. Unused Leak branch omitted.
- modules/iris/background/IrisAfterglowWallpaper.qml and .frag -> corresponding
  Widgets/Iris and Shaders/frag/iris_afterglow_wallpaper.frag. Paths adapted.
- modules/iris/components/IrisLightWash.qml and .frag -> integrated into IrisField.
  Original stops, fall and dither are retained, sampled in output space for the
  shared bar/frame/panel chassis and locally for independent surfaces. The joined
  SDF supplies coverage and the light is composed before the metallic finish;
  no separate rounded-panel overlay or redundant light-wash pass remains.
- Material subset of modules/iris/style/IrisStyle.qml and curated material values
  of modules/iris/settings/IrisThemes.qml -> Widgets/Iris/IrisStyle.qml and
  Helpers/MaterialProfiles.js. Only settings/service inputs and intensity controls
  adapted; no IrisThemes.apply() layout side effects imported.
- modules/iris/style/IrisMood.qml, IrisWashi.qml and services/Lume.qml,
  WallpaperLuma.qml -> Widgets/Iris singletons. Original sampling, palette solving,
  veil/frost and plate composition retained; host services/paths adapted.
- scripts/colors/washi/{main,colour,language,iris,material,washi}.go and three
  upstream regression tests -> Scripts/materials/washi/. Production Go sources
  are unchanged. scripts/colors/washi.sh adapted as Scripts/materials/washi.sh.
- defaults/iris-washi.json -> Assets/Iris/iris-washi.json, unchanged initial palette.
- Necessary luma-grid subset of scripts/images/least_busy_region.py ->
  Scripts/materials/wallpaper_luma.py. Hydra cache paths and letterbox colour adapted.
- Original ColorUtils.mix/relativeLuminance and Places reading-plate equations
  incorporated in IrisStyle/Lume and the Hydra host IrisReadingPlate.
- IrisHostGeometry adapts original explicit host offsets to Umbriel's existing
  window/layer subscription. Reading cards solve with Hydra's secondary ink;
  LauncherHero applies the same original veil/frost solve to its own image crop.

Ryoku revision f7197d72de8a21e44b0bea922bdd915f28f6b327 was inspected as a host
integration reference. Its divergent field/shader implementation was not copied.
No second shell, upstream interface, unrelated service stack or branding is bundled.

Corresponding QML, GLSL, Go and Python sources, compilation launcher and existing
Shaders compilation script accompany the generated QSB files. Preserve these
sources and the required notices/README/About/welcome attribution when distributing.
